# Chunked transfer coding, in both directions.
note a body sent in three chunks becomes one todo
conn
chunked POST /todos {"title":|"sent in |pieces"}
request GET /todos/1
note chunk sizes are hex, extensions are ignored, trailers are read past
conn
send POST /todos HTTP/1.1
send Host: localhost
send Content-Type: application/json
send Transfer-Encoding: chunked
send
send 14;name=value
send {"title":"hex sizes,
send 5
send  ok"}
send 0
send X-Checksum: none
send
request GET /todos/2
note a large file goes out chunked to an HTTP/1.1 client
conn
request GET /docs/big.txt
note and with a content-length to an HTTP/1.0 client, which cannot read chunks
conn
send GET /docs/big.txt HTTP/1.0
send
note a malformed chunk size is a 400 and the connection closes
conn
send POST /todos HTTP/1.1
send Host: localhost
send Transfer-Encoding: chunked
send
send zz
send nope
note a chunk whose data runs past its size is a 400
conn
send POST /todos HTTP/1.1
send Host: localhost
send Transfer-Encoding: chunked
send
send 2
send toolong
send 0
send
note gzip under chunked is not supported
conn
send POST /todos HTTP/1.1
send Host: localhost
send Transfer-Encoding: gzip, chunked
send
